# The one place yojimbo's C library dependencies are versioned.
#
# Columns: name  vendored  tag  minimum
#
#   vendored   the version of the copy in this repository (its VERSION macros)
#   tag        the upstream git tag carrying that version; the -DYOJIMBO_SYSTEM_DEPS CI job
#              installs exactly these tags, so "system dependencies" means the same version the
#              vendored build compiles
#   minimum    the floor a system-installed copy must meet, enforced at configure time
#
# netcode's floor is 1.4.6: SECURITY.md records the connect token handling that lands in
# 1.4.5, and yojimbo's server config passes max_connect_token_lifetime, a field netcode 1.4.4
# and earlier do not have. 1.4.6 raises it again -- yojimbo reads netcode payloads through
# serialize's BitReader, which loads an eight-byte window, and only from 1.4.6 does a payload
# packet carry eight bytes of slack behind the payload, so an older system netcode gives
# yojimbo an out-of-bounds read on packets it accepts. Linking an older system netcode is
# refused rather than warned about. The floor stays below the vendored 1.4.7, whose changes
# yojimbo's sources do not depend on.
# serialize and reliable floor at the vendored version because yojimbo's sources are written
# against it and both define wire formats.
#
# The vendored column is checked against the vendored headers at configure time, so this file
# cannot drift from the tree it describes.

serialize  1.16.2  v1.16.2  1.16.2
reliable   1.4.4   v1.4.4   1.4.4
netcode    1.4.7   v1.4.7   1.4.6
